{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וימשכו", :translit "vayimshěkhú", :gloss "and they drew / and they pulled"} {:he "וימשכו ויעלו את ירמיהו", :translit "vayimshěkhú vehe`ělú et yirmeyáhu", :gloss "and they drew and brought up Jeremiah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וימשכו" "וימשכו ויעלו את ירמיהו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeroth shavah link between two rare identical phrase-openers, reading the second as retributive echo of the first."}], :frame {:text "In Genesis 37:28, the brothers pull Joseph up from the pit. In Jeremiah 38:13, men pull Jeremiah up from the dungeon. Ba'al HaTurim reads the rare repetition of וימשכו as linking the two episodes so that what was done to Joseph is reflected in what later happens to Jeremiah. The midrashic principle of gezeroth shavah connects verses sharing rare words or phrases; cf. the hermeneutic rules enumerated in Shabbat 63a and applied throughout rabbinic literature.", :sources ["Genesis 37:28" "Jeremiah 38:13" "Shabbat 63a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וימשכו" "וימשכו ויעלו את ירמיהו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וימשכו", :refs ["Genesis 37:28" "Jeremiah 38:13"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וימשכו ויעלו את ירמיהו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeroth shavah link between two rare identical phrase-openers, reading the second as retributive echo of the first.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:35.132951583Z", :model "glm-5.2"}